      "title": "Four elements, one application",
      "narration": "Rosa, a self-employed electrician, applies for a medical plan. Her completed application and first premium are the offer. The insurer accepts by issuing the policy as applied for. If the insurer issues it with changes, that is a counteroffer she accepts by paying or keeping it. Consideration flows both ways: Rosa gives premium and truthful statements; the insurer gives its promise to pay covered expenses. Both parties must be competent, meaning of legal age and sound mind, and the contract must have a legal purpose. A contract missing any element is not enforceable.",
